<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Schwarzburg-Rudolstadt</h1><p class="st-meta">1599 CE – 1920 CE · capital Rudolstadt</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Thuringian principality ruled from the Heidecksburg above Rudolstadt, whose last prince was the last German monarch to abdicate in 1918.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The counts of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-schwarzburg">Schwarzburg</a> were among the oldest noble houses of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>. After the death of Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunther-xli-of-schwarzburg-arnstadt">Günther XLI</a> in 1583 and a period of joint rule, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-stadtilm">Treaty of Stadtilm</a> of 1599 divided the County of Schwarzburg between brothers, creating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolstadt">Rudolstadt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sondershausen">Sondershausen</a> lines.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The counts, raised to princes in 1710, ruled two separate blocks of territory, the Upper Lordship around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolstadt">Rudolstadt</a> and part of the Lower Lordship in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>, and gradually shook off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> overlordship. The Lutheran court rebuilt the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidecksburg">Heidecksburg</a> palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> style after a fire in 1735. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friedrich-schiller">Schiller</a> first met <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-wolfgang-von-goethe">Goethe</a> in Rudolstadt in 1788.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Schwarzburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolstadt">Rudolstadt</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-confederation">German Confederation</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a>. Its last prince, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunther-victor-prince-of-schwarzburg">Günther Victor</a>, who had ruled both <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-schwarzburg">Schwarzburg</a> states since 1909, abdicated in November 1918, the last German monarch to do so. In 1920 it merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-state-of-thuringia">Free State of Thuringia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/principality-of-schwarzburg-rudolstadt.jpg" alt="Principality of Schwarzburg-Rudolstadt" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: David Liuzzo Public domainPublic domainfalsefalse This image of simple geometry is ineligible for copyright and there... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_F%C3%BCrstent%C3%BCmer_Schwarzburg.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1599 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rudolstadt</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ludwig Günther I, Günther Victor</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Schwarzburg-Rudolstadt</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1760&amp;focus=principality-of-schwarzburg-rudolstadt" aria-label="Principality of Schwarzburg-Rudolstadt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4938 417 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Schwarzburg-Rudolstadt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5258 673L5249 670M5258 673L5229 694M5258 673L5300 622M5258 673L5250 665"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5249 670h0M5229 694h0M5300 622h0M5250 665h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5258 673h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5258 673h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Rudolstadt. <a href="/atlas?year=1760&amp;focus=principality-of